  "notes": "Event stems from a legacy quality defect traced to the 2013 ANO-1 stator drop accident repair, where inadequate vendor oversight left a bent disconnect tab undetected for years. Cause code X (Other) governs per Block 13 despite narrative describing a clear equipment/quality defect; category kept literally as 'Other' per rule 4. EDG2 and SU-1 transformer both restored power automatically; EDG2 modeled as backup to the vital bus consequence since narrative states it 'started automatically and provided power.' Startup Transformer SU-1 not modeled as a System per rule 6 since it's plant electrical design context providing automatic backup power transfer, not itself part of the failure chain; retained only as a Component note. Previous similar LER 2018-004 emitted as stub per rule 9, using LER number exactly as stated (unit prefix inferred as '1' per plant is ANO-1, but original text just says 'LER 2018-004' with unit clear from context; key formatted as '1-2018-004' consistent with rule 9 example)."
